ted versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.6.stable.official [89cea1439]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable - macOS Sequoia (15.7.3) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M4 Pro (Apple9) - Apple M4 Pro (12 threads) - 24.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using Input.MOUSE_MODE_CONFINED on macOS, moving the mouse until it hits the edge of the screen starts incorrect cursor behavior:\n\n- After the cursor hits the edge, the bug triggers: moving the mouse slowly to the right moves the cursor to the left instead\n- InputEventMouseMotion.relative reports (0, 0) even though InputEventMouseMotion.position is changing\n\nThis reproduces in fullscreen mode and in windowed mode when the window touches a screen border.\nNote: This is not caused by macOS window snapping tools (e.g. Magnet). \n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/87e0d57b-1f9c-47ec-a628-c12ea96a93b7\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Set Input.mouse_mode = Input.MOUSE_MODE_CONFINED \n2. Run the project in fullscreen, or in windowed mode with the window touching a screen edge\n3. Move the mouse until it hits the edge of the screen/window\n4. While the cursor is against the edge, move the mouse slowly to the right\n5. Observe the cursor moving to the left\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mouse_jump_bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25276000/mouse_jump_bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/R